From: prospero-win orbis <noreply@localhost>
Subject: ntdll: orbis: native WoW64 signal entry (0883, 0903) on the PS4

Patches 0883 (raw signal entries through libkernel's syscall stub, the
verified frame, the readiness export) and 0903 (keep the FS base of a
64-bit thread resumed where it was) stay PS5-only in the series. On the PS4
the title measured everything 0883 relies on (ps4-wine phase p2, LOG.md
2026-11-01 18:56): libkernel's getppid stub has the same shape and its
syscall instruction runs other calls; sigaltstack works (with FreeBSD's
stack_t, which wine/orbis/include has); a signal registered with the
kernel's own sigaction and SA_ONSTACK arrives on the alternate stack, where
the entry's 64 KiB round-down finds the thread; the frame holds MXCSR at
ucontext+320+24 and the FS base at +1152.

So their gates take __ORBIS__ too, with two PS4 differences:
- libkernel is found as the module whose code holds getppid's stub, from
  the module list, not by the PS5's handle 0x2001 (the resolver still
  checks the name, libkernel.sprx on the PS4 too, and the stub);
- init_thread_pipe ignores sigaltstack's result, so the readiness caps
  stay 0 unless the main thread's alternate stack is in place and its
  64 KiB-aligned base holds this thread's TEB (PW_NATIVE_ALTSTACK).
The provider's summary line is also logged on the err channel once, so a
title run (WINEDEBUG=err+all) shows why the caps are what they are.

